    "id": "story",
    "type": "story",
    "provenance": "original",
    "title": {
     "en": "What comes next?"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Look at 3, 6, 9, 12. Can you tell what comes next, and why?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pattern",
     "rule",
     "sequence",
     "multiple"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A number pattern follows a rule. In 3, 6, 9, 12 we add 3 each time.\nTo find the rule, look at the difference between neighbouring numbers. If it is always the same, the rule is add or subtract that number.\nIn 1,050, 2,100, 3,150, 4,200 the difference is 1,050. In 5,501, 6,401, 7,301 the difference is 900.\nPatterns can grow by multiplying too: 2, 4, 8, 16 doubles each time.\nMake your own patterns and ask a friend to find the rule.\nPatterns help us predict. If you know the rule you can find any later number."
    }
   },
